   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the racing, pari-mutuel wagering and breeding law, in relation to the distribution of surcharges on off-track winnings",
    "basePrintNo": "S6522",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6522-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §532, RWB L",
    "lawSection": "Racing, Pari-Mutuel Wagering and Breeding Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6522\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the racing, pari-mutuel wagering and breeding law, in\nrelation to the distribution of surcharges on off-track winnings\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nTo extend the current authorization for the distribution of surcharge\nrevenues which will otherwise expire on August 31, 2017.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nThis bill would allow the allocation of specific surcharge revenues to\nthe same racetrack to continue for another five year period.\n\n EFFECT ON CURRENT LAW :\n\nChanges the expiration date from August 31, 2017 to August 31, 2022,\nin keeping with the length of previous extensions.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThis is more a matter of \"housekeeping\" than anything else. Every five\nyears, the provision for the distribution of surcharge earnings from\noff-track winning bets has expired. This year, 2017, is the year\nduring which the last five year extension expires necessitating\nanother extension in order to continue to implement earlier\nagreements. Passage of the last extension was accomplished without a\nnegative vote.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nChapter 365 of 2009 restored an inadvertent omission of the five year\nextension provision from a renumbering and re-ordering of several\nracing law provisions.\n\n2012 - A9260/S6937 - Chap.437\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nTo be determined.\n\n EFFECTIVE :\n\nThis act shall take effect September 1, 2017.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n",
